./test/should-error/assert_not_boolean.pf:6.1-6.26: assert could not evaluate this to true or false; it evaluated to:
	((a = b) or (b = a))
It uses a function, something with no definition (such as a `postulate fun`), or an operation that does not apply (such as an out-of-bounds index).
To reason about it, prove a theorem instead.
